Project-Development
Project Development Phases
Phase 1: Requirement Analysis
Objective: Identify the educational problems to be solved and define the system requirements.
Activities:
•	Study existing AI-based learning assistants and e-learning platforms.
•	Identify student and teacher requirements.
•	Define the main features of EduGenie.
•	Determine hardware and software requirements.
•	Analyze how Google Gemini can be integrated into the application.
Functional Requirements:
•	User registration and login.
•	AI-based question answering.
•	Topic explanation and summarization.
•	Generation of quizzes and practice questions.
•	Personalized learning assistance.
•	Study-plan generation.
•	Educational content recommendations.
•	Conversation/history management.
Deliverable: Software Requirement Specification (SRS).
________________________________________
Phase 2: System Design
Objective: Design the overall architecture and user interface of EduGenie.
Activities:
•	Design the system architecture.
•	Design database structure.
•	Create use-case, activity, sequence, and data-flow diagrams.
•	Design the user interface.
•	Define communication between the application and Gemini API.
Proposed Architecture:
          Student / User
                │
                ▼
       ┌─────────────────┐
       │  EduGenie UI    │
       └────────┬────────┘
                │
                ▼
       ┌─────────────────┐
       │ Application/API │
       │     Backend     │
       └────────┬────────┘
                │
        ┌───────┴────────┐
        ▼                ▼
┌──────────────┐  ┌────────────────┐
│   Database   │  │ Google Gemini  │
│              │  │      API       │
└──────────────┘  └───────┬────────┘
                           │
                           ▼
                  AI-generated response
Deliverable: System architecture, database design, UML diagrams, and UI prototypes.
