Phase 3: Technology Selection and Environment Setup
Objective: Prepare the development environment and select appropriate technologies.
Possible Technologies:
Component	Technology
Frontend	HTML, CSS, JavaScript / React
Backend	Python Flask / Django or Node.js
AI Model	Google Gemini API
Database	MySQL / PostgreSQL / Firebase
Authentication	Firebase Authentication / custom authentication
Development Tool	VS Code
API Testing	Postman
Version Control	Git/GitHub
Activities:
•	Install development tools.
•	Create the project repository.
•	Configure the backend and frontend.
•	Obtain/configure Gemini API credentials securely.
•	Establish database connectivity.
Deliverable: Configured development environment and initial project structure.
________________________________________
Phase 4: Frontend Development
Objective: Develop an intuitive interface through which students can interact with EduGenie.
Modules:
•	Login/Register page.
•	Student dashboard.
•	AI chat interface.
•	Learning topic page.
•	Quiz interface.
•	Study-plan page.
•	Learning history.
•	Profile/settings page.
Activities:
•	Create responsive page layouts.
•	Implement navigation.
•	Develop chat interface.
•	Create forms and interactive components.
•	Add loading, error, and response states.
Deliverable: Functional frontend interface.
________________________________________
Phase 5: Backend Development
Objective: Develop the server-side logic and APIs required by EduGenie.
Activities:
•	Create REST APIs.
•	Implement authentication and authorization.
•	Connect the application to the database.
•	Implement user-profile management.
•	Store conversations and learning activities.
•	Validate incoming requests.
•	Implement error handling.
Example API structure:
POST   /api/auth/register
POST   /api/auth/login
POST   /api/chat
GET    /api/chat/history
POST   /api/quiz/generate
GET    /api/progress
POST   /api/study-plan
Deliverable: Functional backend services.
________________________________________
Phase 6: Google Gemini Integration
Objective: Integrate Gemini's generative-AI capabilities into EduGenie.
Activities:
•	Configure the Gemini API.
•	Develop a service layer for Gemini requests.
•	Create educational prompts.
•	Send student questions to Gemini.
•	Process and display generated responses.
•	Implement contextual conversations.
•	Add prompts for summaries, quizzes, explanations, and study plans.
Example workflow:
Student enters question
          ↓
EduGenie validates request
          ↓
Educational prompt is created
          ↓
Request sent to Gemini
          ↓
Gemini generates response
          ↓
Response processed by backend
          ↓
Answer displayed to student
Deliverable: AI-powered learning assistant.
________________________________________
Phase 7: Educational Feature Development
Objective: Add specialized learning capabilities beyond basic chat.
Major Features:
7.1 AI Tutor
•	Explain difficult concepts.
•	Provide examples.
•	Answer academic questions.
•	Adjust explanations according to the student's level.
7.2 Summarization
•	Convert lengthy content into concise notes.
•	Generate key points.
•	Provide revision-oriented summaries.
7.3 Quiz Generator
•	Generate multiple-choice questions.
•	Generate questions from a selected topic.
•	Provide answers and explanations.
•	Track quiz performance.
7.4 Personalized Study Plan
•	Accept subject/topic and available study time.
•	Generate a structured study schedule.
•	Divide topics into manageable sessions.
7.5 Learning Progress
•	Track completed quizzes.
•	Store learning activity.
•	Display performance information.
•	Identify topics requiring additional practice.
Deliverable: Complete educational functionality.
