Phase 9: Testing
Objective: Verify that EduGenie works correctly, securely, and reliably.
Testing Types:
Testing	Purpose
Unit Testing	Test individual functions/modules
Integration Testing	Test communication between modules
API Testing	Verify backend APIs
UI Testing	Check interface functionality
Database Testing	Verify data storage/retrieval
Performance Testing	Evaluate response behavior
Security Testing	Check authentication and data protection
User Acceptance Testing	Validate usability with target users
Sample Test Case:
Test Case	Input	Expected Result
Login	Valid credentials	User enters dashboard
AI Question	"Explain photosynthesis"	Educational explanation displayed
Quiz	Topic: Mathematics	Quiz questions generated
Invalid input	Empty question	Validation message displayed
History	Existing user	Previous chats displayed
Deliverable: Test report and corrected application.
________________________________________
Phase 10: Security and Optimization
Objective: Improve security, reliability, and performance.
Activities:
•	Secure API credentials using environment variables.
•	Hash passwords rather than storing plain-text passwords.
•	Validate user input.
•	Implement authentication and authorization.
•	Protect APIs from unauthorized access.
•	Add rate limiting where appropriate.
•	Optimize database queries.
•	Handle Gemini/API failures gracefully.
•	Avoid exposing sensitive information in logs.
Deliverable: Secure and optimized application.
